  "narrative": "I use the signed convention consistently: for direction -1 claims, a positive signed estimate means stronger measured dependency in the exposed group, i.e. a more negative raw dependency_composite; for direction +1 claims, a positive signed estimate means a higher/less-negative composite score, i.e. weaker measured dependency. The current supplied-dataset evidence supports five central associations: TP53 loss and KEAP1 loss associate with weaker measured dependency, while MSI-high, SMARCA4 loss, and PTEN loss associate with stronger measured dependency, with PTEN being a moderate rather than near-one-unit effect. Several of these are already internally validated or robust across conditional strata, so the most useful next science is not simply to add more marginal predictors, but to test whether the accepted effects are mutually independent, whether they survive technical and histologic minority strata, whether the moderate PTEN effect remains visible inside other accepted-marker backgrounds, and whether any residual threshold-level predictors remain after excluding the accepted marker axes. I activate H53, SMARCA4 loss within MSI-high cells, and H17, TP53 loss within squamous cells, because these are scientifically meaningful minority-context tests and are expected to have adequate comparison cells despite smaller exposed sizes. The new proposals first add direct conditional estimates for TP53 loss within KEAP1-loss cells and KEAP1 loss within TP53-loss cells, excluding MSI-high cells. These are more interpretable than the rejected/near-null TP53-by-KEAP1 interaction because they quantify whether each accepted effect remains above 0.15 units in the other marker's background. I expect positive signed estimates for both if the effects are largely independent; a near-zero estimate with wide uncertainty would leave context dependence unresolved, while an opposite or clearly subthreshold estimate would make the accepted effect context-sensitive in this dataset. I also add non-Avana library tests for TP53 loss, KEAP1 loss, PTEN loss, and SMARCA4 loss. These test whether the large accepted associations are artifacts of the dominant Avana library or remain detectable in the minority library stratum. Threshold-level effects in non-Avana cells would strengthen broad dataset-level interpretation; subthreshold effects would make the claims library-dependent. I add squamous-cell tests for SMARCA4 loss and KEAP1 loss, in addition to activating TP53 loss in squamous cells, to assess histologic-context robustness beyond the majority adenocarcinoma population. The PTEN proposals test whether the moderate PTEN-loss stronger-dependency association remains threshold-level inside TP53-loss and SMARCA4-loss backgrounds after restricting MSI-high and one other strong marker to reduce masking. Because PTEN is smaller than the large marker effects, attenuation would not necessarily invalidate the accepted main PTEN association, but would make its independence from other accepted axes less certain. Finally, I register residual clean-stratum discovery tests for PIK3CA mutation and SMAD4 loss in cells without TP53 loss, KEAP1 loss, MSI-high, or SMARCA4 loss. PIK3CA mutation is hypothesized to associate with a higher/less-negative composite, but this is genuinely uncertain; SMAD4 loss is hypothesized to associate with stronger dependency, also uncertain. If either crosses threshold with sufficient uncertainty, it becomes a validation candidate; otherwise the accepted-marker axes likely capture most of the signal. No validation is requested in this explore stage; if future results support broad SMARCA4 loss, H43 would be a strong candidate, with H10 MSI-high or H11 TP53 loss as alternative older accepted-marker validation targets. All conclusions remain dataset-level associations, not causal mechanisms or claims of external generalizability.",
  "research_notes": "Updated after iteration 5 explore. Signed convention: direction -1 positive = stronger measured dependency; direction +1 positive = higher/less-negative composite = weaker measured dependency. Current accepted supplied-dataset pattern: MSI_high -> stronger dependency; SMARCA4_loss -> stronger dependency broad; TP53_loss -> weaker/higher; KEAP1_loss -> weaker/higher; PTEN_loss -> moderate stronger. Independently validated accepted claims: H8 PTEN main, H28 PTEN in KEAP1-intact, H40 SMARCA4 in TP53/KEAP1/MSI-negative cells, H13 KEAP1 main reversal. H43 broad SMARCA4 main is accepted from large precise discovery but not yet independently validated; treat context/library/histology results as evidence of robustness. H7 original KEAP1 stronger-dependency direction remains rejected/closed. Negative/closed: lineage subtype main, KRAS, BRAF, MTAP, STK11 overall, MYC, EGFR original stronger-dependency direction, research markers d/e/f, STK11 in KEAP1-intact, RB1 clean, ARID1A clean, BRCA2 clean, ERBB2 clean, TP53 batch_a interaction, KEAP1-by-TP53 interaction, PTEN-by-PIK3CA original interaction. Unresolved/deferred/borderline: CDKN2A H42/H54 near threshold; TP53/MSI interactions H29/H30 small cells; research_signature_a SMARCA4 interaction H57 near-null but wide; H44 SMARCA4-by-lineage interaction deferred. Newly activated via assessments: H53 SMARCA4 within MSI_high, expected exposed cell around 27 if prevalence holds, wide intervals possible; H17 TP53 loss within squamous, adequate cells expected. Active existing pending: H48 MSI_high in clean TP53/KEAP1/SMARCA4-intact cells; H58 APC in clean SMARCA4-intact; H59 NF1 in clean SMARCA4-intact. New iteration 5 proposals prioritize direct context independence, technical/histologic robustness, conditional PTEN, and residual clean-marker discovery. Direct TP53 in KEAP1-loss and KEAP1 in TP53-loss excluding MSI_high test mutual independence; threshold-level directional estimates support independence, near-zero/wide unresolved, opposite/subthreshold context-sensitive. Non-Avana tests TP53, KEAP1, PTEN, SMARCA4 test library dependence; threshold-level non-Avana effects strengthen broad dataset claims, subthreshold effects make claims library-dependent. Squamous tests SMARCA4, KEAP1, and TP53 test histology dependence; minority-stratum support strengthens broadness. PTEN conditional tests within TP53-loss and SMARCA4-loss backgrounds test whether moderate PTEN survives in strong contexts; attenuation is informative but does not necessarily invalidate main PTEN. Residual clean discovery PIK3CA direction +1 uncertain and SMAD4 direction -1 uncertain; if threshold-level, validation candidates; otherwise deprioritize. Validation budget after prior validations: 7 new voluntary validations remaining. Future validation priority after appraise: H43 broad SMARCA4 main if non-Avana/squamous/context checks support robustness; alternative candidates H10 MSI_high and H11 TP53_loss. Keep all claims as dataset-level associations and avoid causal or generalization language."
